TEXT 208 -64 Left 2 ;See voltage at petersen
TEXT 248 -32 Left 2 !va a 0 pwl 0s 450A 1s 450A 1.5s 600A
TEXT 280 -40 Left 2 ;controlled Petersen goes from 450A to 600A after switching on new line
TEXT 312 -16 Left 2 ;Voltage risis slow without wavering\nindicates good compensation\nVoltage has maximal value at best\ncompensation
TEXT -200 80 Left 2 ;From 1.5s till end:\nSwitching on the new line the voltages\nand the currents have transients\nwith higher frequencies. This is called \ncapacitive inrush. The reactive power \nfor charging the new line is fed by the three\nother lines in the circuit. This can be \nshown if you measure the current to \nearth at the four lines. You can see that\nthe currents of the three lines are \noposite to the current at the new switched \nline. You can show this by loading\nthe second .plt file \n(Q_at_SwitchingON_new_line_2.plt)
